  "description": "Jet engine where a front fan accelerates a bypass air stream around the core, producing additional thrust at high propulsive efficiency. High-bypass ratios (5:1 to 12:1) dominate commercial aviation for fuel economy and low noise; low-bypass ratios (0.3:1 to 1:1) serve military fighters requiring high specific thrust.",
